WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
Journey to Silius, we dare you to make the journey.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:26.940
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game in North America.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.960
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.560
And I'm Joe. And normally you say released in North America, so I'm very thrown off.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.420
I know. I caught it.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.340
I caught it too.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.660
And I said that I had a whole other thing I was going to talk about at the top of this episode,

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:42.080
but I guess I'm just rusty.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.820
Yeah. I don't think I can do it.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.720
I don't think I have it in me.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.280
All right. Well, we'll go.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.640
We'll go. Yeah. Thank you.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:52.420
But yeah, thanks for pointing it out right away, Joe, just this way the listeners had no time

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.380
to react on their own.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:54.540
Yeah, that's what I do.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.480
As soon as I'm waiting like a hawk for you to make a mistake.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.680
Yeah, you're basically a listener.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.580
Pretty much the last few episodes I have been.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.140
Yeah. Hey, Ed. Welcome back.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:07.640
Thank you. What I was going to bring up at the top.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:13.260
What were you doing, Joe? I was ill and I had some family things going on.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.380
I don't get it. Oh, okay. You didn't need to go into that.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.520
Yeah. Well, I had to have an answer.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.700
Mike, what were you going to say?

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.440
Yeah. It sounds like Sean's the final boss of Journey to Silius.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:31.480
I was going to say that, you know, to start this episode, I was actually planning on talking

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:38.420
about the box art for this game because I think goes hard isn't the right word, but it

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:42.940
really establishes like a mood and atmosphere for this game before you ever play it.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:46.960
And I'm sure there are other NES boxes that do that.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:55.500
But something about like just the big title being like over to the left, sideways, you

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.200
know, like sideways and just nothing behind it.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:01.360
Just Journey to Silius in this really nice sci-fi font.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:08.660
And then like this beautiful shot of the moon with a, you know, like a Antarctic background

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:14.720
and then like actual NES gameplay stuff like overlaid on that, like stuff you're going to

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.720
see in the game.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.940
It's like, it's a pretty nice work of art.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.860
And I think it really sets up like a good vibe for the game.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.200
I'm not sure if you guys looked into that at all.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:27.180
I mean, I just noticed as soon as I booted this up, I was like, this is, there's some

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.080
great production value all around here.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:34.340
It was very cinematic in the beginning and the beginning of this game piqued my interest.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.280
It's kind of, it's also kind of silly, the beginning of the game.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:46.480
Silly, yes. I would say, yeah, the box art, I don't think we, I haven't seen anything like this before

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:53.200
with, aside from like some of the black box games, I think had some like sprite stuff,

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.380
like really blown up sprite stuff.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:04.500
Whereas since then we've gotten a lot more illustrated and this is kind of like that combination

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:05.300
of the two.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.360
But I think they just know what they're selling here.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:14.660
Like this is just such a good looking game for this, for this system that they're like,

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:15.860
let's put that foot forward.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:21.460
Yeah. And I think that's kind of what you meant too, Joe, about just the opening and everything.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.180
Like presentationally, you know, you're getting not only a good looking game, you're getting

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.440
a good sounding game.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.200
The soundtrack kicks in right away and never really like lets up.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:38.580
Every track on every stage is pretty like intense, rocking, but techno.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:44.940
And they're committed to like, I don't know if they had like design documents or anything,

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.700
but it feels very cohesive.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:52.280
Whereas like in other platformer games, you usually get like, okay, here's the desert level,

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.880
here's the jungle level here.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:58.320
And, you know, and that's fine because you're like going through, you know, like a whole world

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.500
or exploring something.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:06.260
But like, I, I liked the way, uh, that journey feels very cohesive, uh, from the very beginning.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.040
Yeah. Now I have a question and I don't know if this is true.

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:12.380
I'm sure Mike, you might have looked into this.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.700
Was this somehow connected to the Terminator?

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.760
Yes. Okay.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.440
I didn't know. I saw that on the Wikipedia.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:23.980
I'm, uh, I'm, I'm watching, you know, I always just have a YouTube video going while

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:26.160
we're recording these of the game.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.940
And just the first comment, I just saw something about Terminator.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.860
I just looked. And it was like, you could still see some Terminator influence.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:35.020
And I was like, oh, was this supposed to be a Terminator game?

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:39.280
Cause that would make a lot of sense because it feels just like the Terminator future.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.140
You could see some Terminator influence and you can also see some like Xenomorphs at the

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.820
end of the game. Right? Like what's up with that?

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.360
There's like Xenomorphs in everything.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.420
That's what I'm saying though.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:53.500
Right? Like, it's like at this point, if you're, you're either doing Terminator or you're doing,

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:57.980
um, uh, aliens or you're doing another Arnold Schwarzenegger movie, right?

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:03.420
Like everything is just spinning off of the, of that, uh, action genre, which makes sense

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:07.900
on an NES, of course, especially with all those big eighties blockbusters kind of like

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:08.940
reshaping Hollywood.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:13.660
But yes, Joe, it is true that this was supposed to be a Terminator game.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:16.260
Uh, how much of it is still in there?

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:21.340
You know, uh, again, some of the, some of the intro screens.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:28.600
Um, I, can, can we walk through the, the, the intro like cinematic of this game for a

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:29.880
little bit in a second?

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:34.820
Uh, just cause I just wanted to close out the, I just wanted to close out the Terminator

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.720
things. So we don't keep talking about it the whole episode.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:42.720
Uh, the, the long story short is that basically they, uh, either lost the rights or just got

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:47.720
too far out from the release of the movie to justify creating a Terminator game around

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:52.460
it. My guess is that they lost the rights because Terminator is still a big franchise and you

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:54.180
wouldn't just like give that up.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.920
You wouldn't be like, eh, it's just too much time has passed.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.920
I don't think it's worth it. Like, of course you would release a Terminator game.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.100
They released a Jaws game.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:05.820
Um, yeah. Or, or, or just like, uh, uh, what were those three guys that poke each other on the eye?

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:07.720
Three stooges.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:16.060
Yeah. That one. Um, but yeah, this, this intro cinematic, the tone, like, so the visuals are, you know,

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:22.620
they're stunning, but like the tone of what they're saying and the visuals are, are, it's

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:32.300
kind of funny where they show like this very like utopian, uh, blue sky, like future city.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.840
And then you see like a nuclear bomb explode.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:41.460
You got, I mean, you at least got a mushroom cloud and, and then you just see like, oh,

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.760
this guy's dad has passed away.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:50.220
And then later they're like, somebody on the news said that he died.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.780
And it's just like this one guy died after this nuke explode.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:59.080
The, the evening news is going to say that he died after a nuclear incident.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:02.080
Cause the terrorists did a very controlled explosion.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.800
Oh yeah. It looks very controlled.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:07.040
There was a to scale nuclear explosion.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:11.360
So if it fits in your TV, like that's how big it was on that guy.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:17.600
Uh, it is, it is a bit of a weaker plot than the Terminator though.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:22.420
Uh, from, from that point, it's that essentially the character you're playing as, I believe

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.540
his name is Jay, uh, his father is dead.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:32.180
He finds a floppy disk containing, uh, uh, the plans to a project that I guess the terrorists

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.440
were trying to stop.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:35.960
So like space colonization stuff.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:41.480
Yeah. So he has to, uh, you know, basically take down the terrorist and see the project through.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:47.720
So, um, I don't know if we needed, you know, like you always need a story and it, it suffices,

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:54.320
but the actual gameplay, uh, is not about collecting floppy disks or, uh, you know, like your floppy

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.880
disks have like a life meter.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:56.980
Yeah, exactly.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:03.360
Instead it is, uh, a little bit of like a run and gun, but with a lot of platforming as well.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:09.820
Uh, just a pretty straightforward action game left to rights, uh, movement and you play

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:13.300
as Jay McCray, uh, on this mission to defeat the terrorists.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.480
So how is Jay?

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:16.640
What, what's he like?

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:24.200
He's got flowing red locks, um, and a skin tight body suit.

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:29.140
Um, he's, he's got like some nice athleticism to him.

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:30.820
He's very attractive.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:32.940
How does he control Joe?

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:38.820
You read that as like a, a skin tight body suit, like a, like a Spider-Man skin tight.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.140
I read that as like a space suit, like little armor.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.840
Yeah, but it's, you know, it's too low profile.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:47.620
I think, I think it's like kind of shiny and more like spandexy.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:51.340
Hmm. We'll have to, uh, is there any character art?

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:52.720
I don't know.

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:59.280
Um, my, my initial thought of, and I don't know why I, um, still have this.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:05.060
I feel like as, as we've gone through the years, I should have this reaction less frequently,

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:10.860
but I still, when, when there's a character that controls really nicely, I'm still like,

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:13.300
whoa, like this character's controlling nicely.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:16.380
Like I'm just not expecting it, especially in platformers.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:19.040
And we've had a lot more of them as time's gone on.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.980
So I don't know why I'm still not expecting it.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.520
I think I'm just still burned from some earlier games.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:27.800
Um, but yeah, that was my first thought of like, oh, this guy like is fun to play as.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:34.240
Yeah. And, uh, any, does anybody buy that potentially he is John Connor?

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:39.900
I see. I thought that potentially he would have been, I mean, just based on this moment when I found

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.840
out it was term here, he would have been Kyle Reese.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:44.960
I don't know. I guess it would make more sense now that I'm thinking about it.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.880
He'd be John Connor. Cause it's the future, but he just doesn't look like him.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.940
But Kyle Reese was from the future too.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:53.480
That's true. But I was thinking like John Connor, he's just a kid in the eighties.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:57.840
And I like forgot that John Connor was like the, the leader of the resistance.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:09:59.560
Well, they may, okay.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:06.040
They made Kyle Reese or John Connor a redhead and gave him some guns.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.380
So yeah, I mean, I buy that.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:13.280
I feel like Kyle Reese has, is closer to being a redhead than John Connor.

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:14.620
Everyone knows this.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:44.600
I feel like Kyle Reese is a redhead.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:04.760
And guns are the name of the game in this game, because, uh, even, even though it has

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:09.560
like some platforming elements to it and everything, the only way to attack is not with your fist,

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:16.520
but with a gun and you always have, uh, your handgun, which can shoot, uh, pretty rapidly for a handgun.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:23.320
But then you collect, uh, other guns along the way, a shotgun, a machine gun, a homing gun.

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:25.260
I don't know if that's really a thing, but, uh,

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:27.640
Like a homing missile, like launcher thing.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:31.060
Right. Uh, a laser rifle and a grenade launcher.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:35.900
And, uh, the interesting quirk about that is like, yeah, of course all of those are better than a handgun.

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:41.100
So we're going to limit how much you can use those things with a gun gauge.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:47.080
Uh, so you have your, uh, health meter or they're putting a P next to that, either for player or for power.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:48.420
Uh, what do we want to go with?

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:51.460
I'm sure the manual establishes something, but yeah, power sounds right.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:57.260
So you've got your power meter for your health, but then your gun has, uh, essentially bullets,

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:02.440
but you can't really count them like that because they're like the handgun never runs out of bullets.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:04.060
So it's not like you have to think about it like that.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:07.320
It's like alternate gun power.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:13.300
Yeah. Um, and so, you know, you have to use your specialty guns wisely.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:20.780
Um, unlike, uh, you know, or, or kind of similar to a Mega Man situation, you know, where you beat a boss.

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:23.500
I was going to bring, bring up that this felt a bit like Mega Man, yeah.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:28.420
Yeah, because you do have to, in order to get these weapons, you have to beat the, the boss, the sub boss of the stage, right?

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.160
Um, in order to get the weapon.

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:32.160
Oh, if that's the case.

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:33.720
Yeah, like right before the final boss.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:38.600
Yeah. Yeah, I just kind of noticed when I would go to the menu that like, oh, I've got another gun here.

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:40.080
I didn't really associate that with anything.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:43.220
Because you pick up that like, there's like a little bubble that falls in it.

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:44.340
Oh, yeah, with a letter on it.

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:47.180
With a letter in it. I thought it was like, oh, this is just the key to the boss.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.600
It just immediately happens.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:56.980
It's kind of interesting that you get it from the sub boss in order to then use it against the boss of that stage.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:05.180
Like, I guess I appreciate that a little more over the Mega Man system where it's like, you get the gun and you're like, yeah, this would have been great in the fight I just had.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:11.640
Yeah. I mean, that's the thing about like, how you kind of have to manage it in this game though.

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:14.160
Like, you really need to save that.

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:18.420
I mean, there are like, refills.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:20.560
There's like pickups that some enemies will drop.

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:26.820
But you really have a limited amount of usage for these guns and they share a pool.

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:31.480
It's not like you have some for one gun and you can go to the other one.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:41.440
Like, it's just all the guns that aren't the pistol require the same pool of gun gauge.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:50.180
So you end up having to just wait till the boss to use this stuff because you can't really count on there being that many drops.

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:55.160
Yeah, there's very few drops of health for that matter.

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:58.920
Like, the gun one shows up a lot more frequently than the health one does.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:07.820
And so taking damage is probably, you know, like worse than running out of like special.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:15.840
Like, I would rather use my special gun stuff to clear out an enemy than to go into a boss fight with low power.

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:18.920
Mm-hmm. Because you're just not guaranteed to get a lot of that.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:26.880
And the gun thing too, though, like, I don't know, like, just in general, enemies aren't really spawning a lot of these upgrades.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:29.260
Yeah, definitely not.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:39.860
And I found it hard to just from like ease of gameplay, I found it hard to think ahead enough to switch to the gun I need on regular enemies.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:41.000
You know what I mean? Right.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.120
So I was just always kind of rapidly hitting the pistol.

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:51.960
And I honestly think I used the gun more on those sub-bosses, rather the specialty guns on the sub-bosses.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:56.880
Right. Because then I could at least like see, okay, I think I'm about to get to the end of this level here.

00:14:56.960 --> 00:15:01.540
Let me just get something with a little more oomph to it.

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:05.860
And there were some where I was like, okay, I definitely need this gun for this situation.

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:15.040
Now, this isn't true of 100% of the game, but did you notice the reoccurring theme for the most part of the game that you are facing off against one enemy at a time?

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:22.180
I mean, there's definitely sections where they kind of clump up.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:40.600
But there's been, I guess it's usually like one move around enemy and then a couple like turret style enemies or two move around enemies and two turret style enemies.

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:51.560
I felt like it was more like Castlevania style where like you really are just like you're moving to the right and you see like an enemy and you deal with that enemy and then you just go on to the next one.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:57.660
I didn't see too many things other than with turrets where like they might stack up multiple on the screen at a time.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.340
Like, yeah. You know what I mean?

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:06.820
I mean, I was getting like, I was getting surrounded by like some flying stuff and like maybe level two or three.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:10.680
And it turned, this is a kind of difficult game.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.120
It's a very difficult game.

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:27.080
And for me, whether it's that counts as an enemy or not, specifically those like ground turrets that would pop their head up being on the screen at the same time as other enemies were the bane of my existence in this game.

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:36.520
Because I can see the pattern, but it's just hard to really react to that pattern while dealing with an enemy.

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:45.360
I can imagine like getting pretty okay at this game if I really just wanted to memorize spawn locations.

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:49.960
Because like this is a very meticulously like planned game.

00:16:50.160 --> 00:17:01.980
Like you can't just sort of run and gun this like a contra or something because everything is, all these enemies are placed in a spot to like have a gotcha moment.

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:04.600
And you're going to run immediately into fire.

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:08.360
You know, were you noticing that?

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:11.220
Yeah. If you jump down to any platform.

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:13.720
Yeah. Someone's just waiting for you right there.

