00:32:32.600 --> 00:32:39.340
really just comes down to what we were talking about, that sort of memorization that is almost

00:32:39.340 --> 00:32:41.480
required to get good at the game.

00:32:41.480 --> 00:32:47.800
Which is not like a nail in the coffin, like, kiss of death for a game.

00:32:47.900 --> 00:32:53.100
But I do think that that, similar to what you said, Mike, did kind of prevent me from

00:32:53.100 --> 00:32:56.320
having the full amount of enjoyment I could from this game.

00:32:56.720 --> 00:33:00.220
That being said, I think that they really didn't do too much else wrong.

00:33:00.520 --> 00:33:03.440
I mean, this game is really cool and very interesting.

00:33:03.700 --> 00:33:08.880
It's just on the shorter side, and I think that there is a...

00:33:08.880 --> 00:33:15.740
It's like a level of difficulty that didn't sing with me in, like, the sense that it's

00:33:15.740 --> 00:33:17.760
a satisfying, challenging difficulty.

00:33:17.760 --> 00:33:19.700
Some of it was kind of a frustrating difficulty.

00:33:20.940 --> 00:33:23.240
That might just be me being bad at the game.

00:33:23.360 --> 00:33:28.180
But I think overall, it kind of just hovers below Essential for me.

00:33:28.300 --> 00:33:30.240
So, definitely play it, but not Essential.

00:33:30.580 --> 00:33:38.480
Sean? I would just like to state that having a blind drop that has, like, two enemies,

00:33:38.880 --> 00:33:45.040
that you're going to run into and not even really have time to set and react,

00:33:45.620 --> 00:33:49.420
is definitely okay to be frustrated with that.

00:33:49.580 --> 00:33:55.040
You're not bad at video games because you're frustrated with that, is what I would say.

00:33:55.400 --> 00:33:58.980
Thank you. I needed that. I think this game does a little too much of that.

00:33:59.460 --> 00:34:04.080
I think this game didn't take enough of...

00:34:04.800 --> 00:34:11.060
It didn't play around with, like, the gun, like, the upgraded gun mechanic as much as

00:34:11.060 --> 00:34:15.620
I think it should. I think maybe you should have had a little bit more time to play around with those because

00:34:15.620 --> 00:34:19.200
right now it's just too situational.

00:34:20.720 --> 00:34:23.960
And I think it should have been a bit longer.

00:34:24.860 --> 00:34:26.660
I'm agreeing with both you guys.

00:34:26.760 --> 00:34:33.420
I had a lot of fun with this game when I wasn't going down those blind pitfalls and getting

00:34:34.940 --> 00:34:36.900
really, really hardcore hit.

00:34:38.140 --> 00:34:45.340
But I think if they just changed the vibe a little bit, like, just make it a little longer,

00:34:46.080 --> 00:34:51.220
give your guns a little bit more ammo, that in turn makes the game a little bit more forgiving,

00:34:51.840 --> 00:34:54.180
and so now you've got the same amount of...

00:34:54.180 --> 00:34:58.920
Like, it's just, like, it's so compressed that it really needs to be something that you

00:34:58.920 --> 00:35:06.020
memorize, whereas if you could just be a little bit more freeform with it, a little bit looser,

00:35:06.020 --> 00:35:09.300
then I think it would be a better game for it.

00:35:09.680 --> 00:35:13.040
I'm rambling. It's a play it, not an essential game.

00:35:13.300 --> 00:35:18.800
It's kind of funny, though, if this game was released, you know, as an indie game in 2025,

00:35:19.600 --> 00:35:20.760
it would be...

00:35:20.760 --> 00:35:25.240
It would play and behave and control mostly the way that it's laid out here.

00:35:25.420 --> 00:35:29.580
Like, they made a great game, especially for that time, but, like, one that still plays

00:35:29.580 --> 00:35:35.280
well. It would just be that you would actually be able to clear through the enemies and there would

00:35:35.280 --> 00:35:38.100
be more health and, like, you would get through it, right?

00:35:38.100 --> 00:35:41.780
It would be a little challenging, but you'd get through everything and experience everything

00:35:41.780 --> 00:35:47.160
there is to offer. Games are now, like, more focused on that, where it seems like, obviously, back in the

00:35:47.160 --> 00:35:50.560
day, you know, we're talking about making it hard just way it lasts longer, but I also

00:35:50.560 --> 00:35:52.080
just don't think, like...

00:35:52.080 --> 00:35:57.360
I don't think developers really cared if you ever got to the end of their games, right?

00:35:57.500 --> 00:35:58.980
Like, that wasn't really the point of it.

00:35:59.160 --> 00:36:02.060
They obviously didn't care on this one because they didn't really put anything there.

00:36:02.480 --> 00:36:04.340
Yeah. They'll put you back around.

00:36:05.060 --> 00:36:10.680
Right, right, you know? So, it's kind of funny to think, like, nowadays, there's so much about, like, a complete experience

00:36:10.680 --> 00:36:15.840
and, you know, like, I think people would be mad if they bought, like, even a AAA game,

00:36:15.960 --> 00:36:20.080
but even an indie game, if they bought it, not knowing that it was going to be hard and

00:36:20.080 --> 00:36:24.080
just being, like, this old-school NES hard, I don't think that's what people are looking

00:36:25.300 --> 00:36:27.600
to play with these new games.

00:36:27.600 --> 00:36:31.900
I think about even just something like The Messenger to Ninja Gaiden.

00:36:32.060 --> 00:36:37.780
Like, The Messenger is very much like Ninja Gaiden, but it's a game that anybody with, like,

00:36:38.020 --> 00:36:41.720
